<title>BELGIUM: EU's de Silguy denies report on Italy's EMU entry.</title>
<headline>EU's de Silguy denies report on Italy's EMU entry.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commissioner for monetary affairs, Yves-Thibault de Silguy, denied on Monday the Commission was studying how to keep Italy out of a single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>Responding to an Italian magazine article over the weekend that said such a report had been prepared by the Commission, due in large part to German worries, de Silguy said no such paper existed.</p>
<p>&quot;There is on Commission document on this subject,&quot; he told a news conference following a meeting of EU finance ministers.</p>
<p>&quot;I searched high and low this morning.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6830</p>
